\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Interaction representations and geometric readouts.} (a) Human-surface depth ratios initialize scene scale; Body-Anchored Scene Query relates 24 body anchors to local scene features, forming a metric interaction representation for residual scale and bias prediction. (b) Hierarchical Context Attention pools self-surface and environmental evidence across four supports around 96 body regions, forming regional interaction representations for whole-body translation proposals. Reprojecting and resampling after an update recomputes the relations for the next placement readout. Pose and shape are preserved.}}{19}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:method-detail}{{7}{19}{\textbf {Interaction representations and geometric readouts.} (a) Human-surface depth ratios initialize scene scale; Body-Anchored Scene Query relates 24 body anchors to local scene features, forming a metric interaction representation for residual scale and bias prediction. (b) Hierarchical Context Attention pools self-surface and environmental evidence across four supports around 96 body regions, forming regional interaction representations for whole-body translation proposals. Reprojecting and resampling after an update recomputes the relations for the next placement readout. Pose and shape are preserved}{figure.7}{}}
